; Stage 15 W5c: widening the `defvar` string-literal gate from `TY-PTR` to
; `is-ptr-like` admits `CStr` — it must NOT admit anything else. A string
; literal in an integer-typed global is still rejected, at its own line, and the
; diagnostic now names the offending type.
(defvar g:i32 "not a pointer")

(defn main ():i32
  (return g))
